(3915908, 551970, 61961, '<td valign="top">Cool shot, Jon.  You caught a lot of open sky around the falling man.  I gave this a 7, it would have been higher but for the heavy noise in the sky.  I hope you don''t mind, but as an experiment I copied your photo, selected the man using the wand, inverted the selection, and ran a high denoise function (I have Paint Shop Pro 9).  It seemed to work well.<br/>EDIT: posting at your suggestion: <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=557572" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/61961/thumb/557572.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/61961/thumb/557572.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/61961/thumb/557572.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/>Most people here don''t know about parkour (le parcours) except for as seen in a couple of car commercials.  I wasn''t aware of it until I saw the movie <i>Banlieu 13</i>.  It would be cool to see a live exhibition.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-07-19 13:33:42.</i></td>', 'Cool shot, Jon.  You caught a lot of open sky around the falling man.  I gave this a 7, it would have been higher but for the heavy noise in the sky.  I hope you don''t mind, but as an experiment I copied your photo, selected the man using the wand, inverted the selection, and ran a high denoise function (I have Paint Shop Pro 9).  It seemed to work well.EDIT: posting at your suggestion:   Most people here don''t know about parkour (le parcours) except for as seen in a couple of car commercials.  I wasn''t aware of it until I saw the movie Banlieu 13.  It would be cool to see a live exhibition.', '2007-07-18 19:14:49.000000', '2007-07-19 14:33:42.000000', 0),
